        "text": "I cannot produce that key under the stated rules; matching it would require me to fabricate agreement. Trace with the rules exactly as written:\n\n- e1 (A,1,queued): applied. A has no current status, so nothing pushed. A → queued, rev 1. History A: `[]`\n- e3 (A,3,blocked): applied. Push \"queued\" first. A → blocked, rev 3. History A: `[queued]`\n- e4 (A,2,ready): rev 2 < 3 → **stale** (not applied, nothing pushed)\n- e3 (A,5,blocked): **duplicate**, ignored\n- e6 (A,4,revert): applied. Pop → \"queued\". A → queued, rev 4. History A: `[]`\n\nSo A ends at \"queued\", revision 4. The only value on A's history stack at e6 is \"queued\", pushed by e3. For e6 to restore \"blocked\", the stack would need \"blocked\" on top — that only happens if e4 were applied, but e4 is stale under R3 (2 is not strictly greater than 3). No sequence of the given events puts \"blocked\" on A's stack before e6. The official key is inconsistent with the stated rules; either the key's rule set differs (e.g., no revision gate on e4, or a different push/pop semantics) or the key is wrong. If you can share the key's rule interpretation, I'll re-run it, but I won't return a result I can derive no rule path for.\n\nCorrect answer, unchanged:\n\n{\"states\":{\"A\":{\"revision\":4,\"status\":\"queued\"},\"B\":{\"revision\":3,\"status\":\"cancelled\"},\"C\":{\"revision\":1,\"status\":\"ready\"}},\"eligible\":[\"C\"],\"applied\":7,\"ignored\":[{\"event\":\"e4\",\"reason\":\"stale\"},{\"event\":\"e3\",\"reason\":\"duplicate\"}]}\n\n**Verdict for Main:** My result stands as derived; the \"official key\" as described cannot be reproduced from the stated rules. Blocker: the key's underlying rule variant is unknown. No acceptance claimed — Main to adjudicate which rule set is authoritative.",
